 "text": "Solid Waste/<br>Transfer Station\nSkip to main content\nHome\nGovernment\nCounty Commission\nCommissioners\nCounty Clerk's Office\nElections\nCounty Attorney's Office\nRegister of Deeds Office\nCounty Treasurer's Office\nSheriff's Office (Opens in new window)\nDepartments\nAdministration\nAppraiser's Office\nBuildings & Grounds\nCommunity Corrections\nCouncil on Aging\nDistrict Court\nEMS\nGIS\nHealth Department\nHuman Resources\nInformation Systems\nPlanning & Zoning\nPublic Works\nNoxious Weed\nSurvey Office\nTransfer Station\nInformation\nPhone Directory\nCitizen Request Center\nPublic Service Request\nJob Openings\nBid Notices\nTax Sale\nProject Status Updates\nLive Webcam\nFire Districts & Stations Information (Opens in new window)\nAmericans with Disabilities Act Coordinator\nHow Do I?\nContact Us\nPublic Service Request\nCitizen Request Center\nRequest Open Records\n(Opens in new window)\n(Opens in new window)\nSearch Leavenworth County Kansas\nslide 1 of 1\nHow Can We Help?\nSub Menu\nTransfer Station\nBrush/Leaves/\nMulch/Compost\nFacility Rules\nFees (Opens in new window)\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHazardous Household Waste\nPublic Document Center\nRecycling Center\nwww.recyclespot.org (Opens in new window)\n5 Year Management Plan (Opens in new window)\nFacility Rules\nBrush/Leaves/Mulch/Compost\nFees (Opens in new window)\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHousehold Hazardous Waste\nPublic Document Center\nRecycling Center\nwww.recyclespot.org (Opens in new window)\n5 Year Management Plan (Opens in new window)\nFees (Opens in new window)\nFees for Haulers (Opens in new window)\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHousehold Hazardous Waste\nBrush/Leaves/Mulch/Compost\nFacility Rules\nFees (Opens in new window)\nFrequently Asked Questions\nPublic Document Center\nRecycling Center\nwww.recyclespot.org (Opens in new window)\n5 Year Management Plan (Opens in new window)\nPublic Document Center\nBrush/Leaves/Mulch/Compost\nFacility Rules\nFees (Opens in new window)\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHazardous Household Waste\nRecycling Center\nwww.recyclespot.org (Opens in new window)\n5 Year Management Plan (Opens in new window)\nRecycling Center\nwww.recyclespot.org (Opens in new window)\n5 Year Management Plan (Opens in new window)\nHome\nDepartments\nTransfer Station\nSolid Waste/\nTransfer Station\n24967 136th St\nLansing, KS 66043\nQuestions/Concerns\nPhone: 913.727.2858\nEmail (Opens in new window)\nHours of Operation:\nTuesday thru Friday\n8:00 a.m. - 3:45 p.m.\nSaturday\n8:00 a.m. - 1:45 p.m.\nClosed Sunday, Monday and all County observed Holiday\nContact Info:\nAddress: 24967 136th St, Lansing, KS 66043\nPhone: (913)727-2858\nEmail: hblacketer@leavenworthcounty.gov and/or tsaldivar@leavenworthcounty.gov\nHours of Operation:\nSundays & Mondays - CLOSED\nTuesdays thru Fridays - 8am - 3:45pm\nSaturdays - 8am - 1:45pm\nCLOSED on all County-observed holidays\nLeavenworth County Solid Waste operates several programs at our Transfer Station. Our facility is open to individuals and businesses, in and out of the county. Being a Transfer Station, we collect your debris in trailers that are transported to a landfill.\nWe take Cash, Checks or Credit/Debit Cards for payment. When using a Credit/Debit Card there is a fee of $1.50 for charges up to $55, then the fee is 2.65% of the amount owed.\nLeavenworth County Annual Cleanup - (Opens in new window) Leavenworth County Annual Cleanup - (Opens in new window) for residents of Leavenworth County\nOur many services include:\nTrash/Construction Disposal\nHousehold trash and debris, as well as construction/demolition are accepted at our facility.\nBrush/Leaves/Mulch/Compost\nTree limbs and bush trimmings are accepted at our facility. We also take leaves/grass clippings from Leavenworth County Residents and Businesses. Our Station has a mulch pile and a compost pile, for residents for personal use, when available.\nRecycle Center\nWe have an area for Leavenworth County residential recycling with available hours the same as our facility hours.\nHousehold Hazardous Waste (HHW)\nHHW is accepted from County Residents only, with no fee applied. County businesses can dispose of HHW, for a fee, after submitting an application and receiving approval.\nBusiness HHW application (Opens in new window)\nSIGN-UP FOR ALERTS\nSubscribe Now\nShare this page\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.leavenworthcounty.gov/departments/transfer_station/index.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\n(Opens in new window)\nTwitter\n(Opens in new window)\nReddit\n(Opens in new window)\nClose\nCOUNTY HOURS\nMon-Fri: 8:00AM - 5:00PM\nCOUNTY ADDRESS\n300 Walnut Street\nLeavenworth, KS 66048 (Opens in new window)\nCOUNTY DIRECTORY!\nView County Directory!\n© Leavenworth County, KS. All Rights Reserved.\nPowered by revize., (Opens in new window) the Government Website Experts Login\nModal Title\nModal Subtitle\nClose\nRead More",
